{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520363817,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDg5NTIyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370895227"},"message":"yes, this \"Feature\" came up with fresh 0.9.2 release from two days ago.  Some git operations really dislike having no git user.name/email configured. So now instead of waiting for things to break/work inconsistently we ask to configure git first","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520363827,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1MDcyODkwNDA="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520364771,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDkwMDE0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370900141"},"message":"I think we have rushed it a bit... man git-commit-tree describes:\n```\n       While parent object ids are provided on the command line, author and\n       committer information is taken from the following environment\n       variables, if set:\n\n           GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\n           GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\n           GIT_AUTHOR_DATE\n           GIT_COMMITTER_NAME\n           GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL\n           GIT_COMMITTER_DATE\n\n       (nb \"\u003c\", \"\u003e\" and \"\\n\"s are stripped)\n\n       In case (some of) these environment variables are not set, the\n       information is taken from the configuration items user.name and\n       user.email, or, if not present, the environment variable EMAIL, or, if\n       that is not set, system user name and the hostname used for outgoing\n       mail (taken from /etc/mailname and falling back to the fully qualified\n       hostname when that file does not exist).\n```\nso us checking for config settings only is a bit \"too crude\".\nI think, if config vars aren't defined do a quick check by issuing \"git init; git commit\" in a temp dir and detect complaints (I do not think it would be practical to track).  And then if we detect a problem we should either\n- retain current behavior and demand configuration which still will not be friendly to \"consumer\" use cases as @djarecka where authorship on commits annex etc does isn't really important\n- issue a warning, and proceed while defining a fake name/email variables (e.g. \"DataLad User\" for name and \"datalad-user@example.com\" for email) from aforementioned to be used during calls to git.  This way \"real\" users would get informed that something went wrong and bots could proceed with their needs without requiring some artifactual configuration\n\n@datalad/developers  what do you think?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520402778,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTAzMzQ1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2273#issuecomment-371033450"},"message":"Thought about this more, and realized that the datalad_core extractor should put this into the dataset metadata it produces (or should produce). Along with a whole bunch of other info. For `isPartOf` we need to get #2278 resolved in order to make it nice and smooth.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520532815,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1MTE3MjkzOTY="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531008,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMTEzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2273#issuecomment-374501133"},"message":"Please see #2326 for a related RF.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531033,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMTIyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2273#issuecomment-374501220"},"message":"Also see #2290","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1522008338,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUzOTc0NjA1Ng=="},"status":2}]}